{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred","id":1487744,"title":"Which path of Enlightenment is the most practical for kindred?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-24T11:02:15-07:00","id":1487744,"title":"Which path of Enlightenment is the most practical for kindred?","content":"I still think it's the Path of Harmony, for reasons I think is obvious. (<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_Harmony\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Path_of_Harmony</a>)<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:25:34-07:00","id":1487750,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Harmony or Feral Heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:55:14-07:00","id":1487756,"title":"","content":"For <b>Harmony</b> I disagree because of Sins 2, 4 and 7. 2 - Feeling guilty about killing when necessary, has the problem of not really being something under your control. It the Path is not helping you to not feel guilt, but instead demanding that you don't, then it is a really hard command to follow, and at level 2 nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Sins 4 and 7 have the problem of being too open to interpretation, and that isn't necessarily your own interpretation. What is pointless, how much is too much? Those are questions that an ethical path should answer, not ask and then punish you based on which answer you find elsewhere. Depending on the ST it may really be a piece of cake, but just having distinct interpretation from your ST may be grounds to having a really hard time with the Path (I don't worry so much about those above 7 because then you're talking Paragons).<br /> <br /> And <b>Feral Heart</b> is easier, but still has similar problems on interpretation with Sins 2 to 4, which again is a problem because of how low they are. While it is less likely to be an issue, it is still too open to interpretation for too low, which means basic, tenets. When does need counts for a follower of the Path? How do you define survival? What counts as an instinct? While those are less dubious, they're still too open, specially under STs that are either too inexperienced or just kinda jerks. And if things get too complicated, then even level 1 may become too much of a burden as the player can't say when a death is necessary and when it isn't (or just end up with the ST calling Degeneration anyways).<br /> <br /> Now, if we take the overall idea and ditch the current rules, just comparing their ethics and assuming a corpus of philosophers that really help with understanding their nuance, then I would completely side with <b>Harmony</b> being the winner by far (and <b>Feral Heart</b> loses position do to the principles on it that are not codified on the rules.<br /> <br /> But within the current classic RAW (as V5 have no official RAW on Paths), I have to say that sorry, but the most practical and easier to follow is, hands down, <b>Humanity</b>. It is the easiest to understand in the modern world even if you don't particularly follow it or its ethical principles, and the level of active effort necessary to really fall too low is huge. It shouldn't be like that and I think this is a design flaw, but really it is the most practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:11:44-07:00","id":1487759,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Kindred I must say, but Harmony is indeed the &quot;best&quot;<br /> Via Consuasor, commonly called the Path of the Vizier is nice too<br /> But personally, my all time favorite and most practical in my eyes is te Via Venator Umbra, the Path of the Grey Hunter; a perfect path for a civilized city predator, wich technically every Cainite in their heart","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:56:22-07:00","id":1487765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487759#post1487759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Kindred I must say, but Harmony is indeed the &quot;best&quot;<br /> Via Consuasor, commonly called the Path of the Vizier is nice too<br /> But personally, my all time favorite and most practical in my eyes is te Via Venator Umbra, the Path of the Grey Hunter; a perfect path for a civilized city predator, wich technically every Cainite in their heart</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This feels like a path that would be very suitable for gangrel with presence, protean and auspex. Suprised there isnt a bloodline like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:03:10-07:00","id":1487767,"title":"","content":"Find a single functional definition of &quot;practical,&quot; or it's all just opinion anyway.<br /> <br /> I, for example, struggle accepting any Instinct Path as &quot;the most practical,&quot; because Frenzies are impractical and Instinct only lets you avoid the weakest sources of them. &quot;I can ignore Frenzy stimuli of difficulty 2 or 3, but 4+ and I always auto-Frenzy,&quot; in terms of practicality, is far harsher a thing to deal with than some of the stricter Paths sin hierarchies out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-24-2022, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:44:55-07:00","id":1487774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487756#post1487756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Harmony</b><br /> <br /> I disagree because of Sins 2, 4 and 7. 2 - Feeling guilty about killing when necessary, has the problem of not really being something under your control. It the Path is not helping you to not feel guilt, but instead demanding that you don't, then it is a really hard command to follow, and at level 2 nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who follow the path tend to be more animalistic in nature, they dont see the practicality in good and evil, and simply do what they need to survive. If someone dies, well it was bound to happen sooner or later, feeling bad about it is not going to change that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487756#post1487756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sins 4 and 7 have the problem of being too open to interpretation, and that isn't necessarily your own interpretation. What is pointless, how much is too much? Those are questions that an ethical path should answer, not ask and then punish you based on which answer you find elsewhere. Depending on the ST it may really be a piece of cake, but just having distinct interpretation from your ST may be grounds to having a really hard time with the Path (I don't worry so much about those above 7 because then you're talking Paragons).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the practioners will understand when they are being too kind and when they are being too cruel. Picking up someones keys is different than running into a burning building to save them. Similar to how making a cruel remark about someone is different from going full tzmisce on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487756#post1487756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And <b>Feral Heart</b> is easier, but still has similar problems on interpretation with Sins 2 to 4, which again is a problem because of how low they are. While it is less likely to be an issue, it is still too open to interpretation for too low, which means basic, tenets. When does need counts for a follower of the Path? How do you define survival? What counts as an instinct? While those are less dubious, they're still too open, specially under STs that are either too inexperienced or just kinda jerks. And if things get too complicated, then even level 1 may become too much of a burden as the player can't say when a death is necessary and when it isn't (or just end up with the ST calling Degeneration anyways).</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres no need to randomly kill a mortal minding their buisness on the streets, but there will be a need to kill them if they are a masquerade breach/hunters/in self defence.<br /> <br /> Survival is what you need to do to see another night. You need blood to survive, you may need to kill a mortal to get that blood.<br /> <br /> Instinct is behaviour that is hard wired into us. A vampires fear of fire and the sun can be cinsidered instinct. Fear is considered instinct, if you suddenly find yourself up against a werewolf and you run out of fear, thats instinct.<br /> <br /> <br /> I may be the odd one out, but to me it seems like something that should not require much thought from the practitioners of these paths. Now if the ST in question is having trouble with it, well, I guess just stick with what they are most comfortable with and roll with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:26:23-07:00","id":1487781,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that Harmony (and plenty of other Paths) maintain the false idea that humans are not animals with instincts; and thus lots of things humans do for survival are listed as not proper.<br /> <br /> Harmony (while only a sin at higher levels) argues that society is bad. But society is a highly effective survival strategy for both vampires and humans. Humans have very strong instincts as social animals that power societies and vastly increase survival. Harmony is essentially hypocritical by denying the natural urges of both humans and vampires to think in long terms (as part of survival for both), while advocating for following natural urges.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:29:58-07:00","id":1487782,"title":"","content":"<i>via Regalis</i> for the true noble kindred hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:35:25-07:00","id":1487783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487782#post1487782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>via Regalis</i> for the true noble kindred hahaha</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Sips blood out of a wine glass.*<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://wompampsupport.azureedge.net/fetchimage?siteId=7575&amp;v=2&amp;jpgQuality=100&amp;width=700&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fi.kym-cdn.com%2Fphotos%2Fimages%2Fnewsfeed%2F001%2F474%2F943%2Fb12.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:43:06-07:00","id":1487784,"title":"","content":"Road of the Devil<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:52:43-07:00","id":1487786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487784#post1487784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Road of the Devil<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/mobile/000/030/710/dd0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-24-2022, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:59:55-07:00","id":1487788,"title":"","content":"Most practical from which perspective? <br /> <br /> If you're talking being a Hunter Gatherer predator, the above mentioned Feral Heart or Harmony may be best. <br /> <br /> If you're talking the life cycle of your average Camarilla Cainite, that would probably be Humanity for a century or two, switching to Path of Power and the Inner Voice or Path of Honorable Accord when Humanity drops to 4 or so. Though the Road of Kings variants from Dark Ages would fit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:51:00-07:00","id":1487816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487774#post1487774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be the odd one out, but to me it seems like something that should not require much thought from the practitioners of these paths. Now if the ST in question is having trouble with it, well, I guess just stick with what they are most comfortable with and roll with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, you don't need to explain those Paths to me, I don't think you understood my point.<br /> <br /> 1 - You don't control your feelings. Stating the Path's rationale behind making a feeling into a sin doesn't change that you don't control your feelings. And if the Path states a feeling as a sin, then the Path already assumes that you're not achieving immunity to your own emotions just because you're following the Path and assuming its rationale. A Path sin is, by definition et necessity, something a person following it is still prone to commit.<br /> <br /> How do you define when the character feels something? Usually this is completely up to the player, but not always. Not only powers can directly mess with your feelings (forcing you into a level 2 sin, nonetheless), sometimes character feelings are dictated by the ST or by a dice roll for whatever story purpose at the moment. Those aren't usually relevant because they have no direct weight in the mechanics, but a Path that makes a feeling into a sin basically forces this to become a relevant question.<br /> <br /> Is there a need for some hard rule on feelings or for the ST to press on the matter? Unless it becomes a problem, like if Degeneration is being a strong theme and the other players are feeling at a big disadvantage because you got a cheat code Path, I don't think so. And I don't think many chronicles would end up like that.<br /> <br /> But what I would do or what you would do doesn't matter as much as the fact that the rules of the Path leave this in the air, and so any ST can answer the question however they want and it will be valid within the game. The whole idea of discussing the matter only makes sense if we take into account that the game is open for anyone to play, and so the material must be evaluated with other interpretations being accounted for.<br /> <br /> Not only that, Paths are meant to put ideologies into game terms, and that means that sins exist in terms of behavior/decisions that can be observed in the game. A subjective feeling is an extremely poor fit as a sin, no matter how much it is relevant to the ideas that inform the sin.<br /> <br /> 2 - What the practitioners will understand or not isn't relevant, they're figments of our imagination. What <b>we</b> will understand or not, and if we're able to understand the same thing, is what matters. And making examples with really easy to differentiate situations does not really help when things get complicated and open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> Those aren't abstract questions during the game, they're things that affect real decisions by the characters. <b>Your</b> interpretation of your Path informs your strategies and decisions to deal with the things that happen at the game, but the <b>ST's</b> interpretation define when your character is going to roll for Degeneration. A disconnect between the two means that you can't take informed decisions by yourself, since you can't know their results by yourself.<br /> <br /> Simple on paper, messy in practice. If the Prince orders you to kill someone that doesn't threaten you in any other way, what is the right thing to do under the Path? Does the order of the Prince itself consists of enough threat to justify the kill? What if you don't know what the consequences will be, you can just imagine? There are many situations in the game when killing is a smart move, but asking if it is a <i>necessary</i> move under the purview of an ethical code is a whole different matter. And unless you're happy at level 2, <b>Feral Heart</b> leaves you in those situations with a very tricky question, as you have to guess what the ST will deem the right answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487781#post1487781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that Harmony (and plenty of other Paths) maintain the false idea that humans are not animals with instincts; and thus lots of things humans do for survival are listed as not proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but not quite a problem.<br /> <br /> All in all, the point of the Paths is to give the characters a protecting philosophy for their ego, not to be right or sound under scrutiny. And while that would probably be better, I don't thing it is a necessity in the setting given how many are actively used as social and as political tools, and that in the end their grasp on your Beast is more important than their intellectual honesty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487784#post1487784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Road of the Devil</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> The very first sin of never encouraging virtue or aiding its agents makes the whole thing unsustainable, as whenever this very broad definition is also what will help you to do the other things, which in any, even barely, functional society is a given from time to time, you'll be required to either break all the other tenets or commit a level 1 sin.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but the original <b>Road of the Devil</b>/<b>Sin</b> is one of the few DA Roads that are irredeemably stupid.<br /> <br /> And if you're instead referring to the modern <b>Path of the Devil</b>, then it is pretty standard on how hard and impractical it is to follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T18:48:26-07:00","id":1487823,"title":"","content":"Path of Typhon. Just make sure you don't forget to say your prayers to daddy Set before you go to sleep in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T19:02:14-07:00","id":1487825,"title":"","content":"As I said, Path of Kings is the best by a mile. After all, it's made for rulers of the night, if one doesn't feel comfortable with its tenets, then it means one is bound to serve lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T19:57:25-07:00","id":1487832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487823#post1487823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Path of Typhon. Just make sure you don't forget to say your prayers to daddy Set before you go to sleep in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only big problems are the level 2 and 8 sins. Failing to take advantage of a weakness in a void, without considering if it is the smartest decision in context, is a big problem for a level 2 sin. Adding an &quot;at an appropriate time&quot; would improve it a lot.<br /> <br /> Destroying vampires in Golconda regardless is overall a bad tenet from a practical standpoint, be it as in practical to accomplish the intent if the Path or practical in easing your own life and teaching you valuable wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487744-which-path-of-enlightenment-is-the-most-practical-for-kindred?p=1487825#post1487825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, Path of Kings is the best by a mile. After all, it's made for rulers of the night, if one doesn't feel comfortable with its tenets, then it means one is bound to serve lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly extremely suitable to someone with the right mindset. The Oaths can become tricky to deal with, but if you want to be a successful leader then managing your fealty and your promises just comes with the territory (sometimes literally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}